    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d419">

                <pb facs="0921" n="889" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v15/pg889"/>

                <head>419. Memorandum of a Telephone Conversation Between the President and the
                    Secretary of State, Washington, June 19, 1958, 6:10 p.m.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d419-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1958-06-19T18:10:00-04:00"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">June 19, 1958, 6:10
                    p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>The Sec said we are having a rough time with Garcia on the communiqué and he will
                    have a draft to show him at dinner tonight. What we have got is a 75 million
                    dollar Ex-Im Bank Credit and a 50 million dollar for development loan contingent
                    upon our getting the requisite funds from Congress and then there would be if
                    and when we get it, though we are not saying anything about it in the
                    communiqué, 25 million dollars on this gold claim. They have a 3-year 300
                    million dollar program and this meets their purposes which Garcia <pb
                        facs="0922" n="890" xml:id="pg890"/> admits but he wants to be able to
                    mention 200 million even though they don’t spend it. There is no way of getting
                    it and it would not be in good faith with a side agreement that he would not
                    call for it. The Sec thinks we should stand firm. G<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d419-f2"/> pretends to be unhappy. Bohlen thinks he probably is
                    satisfied and should be. He will press the Pres tonight so you will probably
                    have an unpleasant time of it. The Pres said the answer to him is we cannot
                    promise money that is not appropriated and authorized. We have to work on a
                    yearly basis and have to keep good faith with the Congress as with him. The Sec
                    will bring a draft<anchor n="3" xml:id="d419-f3"/> to dinner.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
